=== HOOK_PORT ===
useWatch.ts: NO CHANGES
  - All URLs already have no /api/v1 prefix:
    /watch/summary?vehicle_id={n}, /watch/complication?vehicle_id={n}, POST /watch/command
  - All query params + body fields already snake_case (vehicle_id, command)
  - WatchSummary interface is INLINE in useWatch.ts (kept inline per Phase-43/0036 OnboardingStatus
    type-source decision: only one feature consumer + one dashboard widget consume it; both read the
    snake_case wire shape directly).
  - WatchSummaryWidget.tsx (web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/, OUT OF SCOPE) imports
    useWatchSummary + useWatchComplication and reads summary.range_km / inside_temp_c which match
    the inline interface field names — wire-shape-compatible, no widget changes needed.
=== PAGE_PORT ===
WatchFacePage.tsx: ported 2 SI fields
  - data.range_km (km on the wire; backend computes RatedRange*1.60934 in watch_handler.go:245)
    -> convertDistanceFromSI(data.range_km * 1000, unitPrefs.distance)
    -> displayed as Math.round(displayRange) + unitPrefs.distance suffix in BatteryGauge
    BatteryGauge prop signature changed: rangeKm -> rangeDisplay (already converted) +
    distanceUnit: DistanceUnitPref (suffix label).
  - data.inside_temp_c (deg C on the wire) -> convertTempFromSI(data.inside_temp_c, unitPrefs.temperature)
    -> displayed as Math.round(displayInsideTemp) + bare degree glyph for watch-face minimalism
    (user already knows their preferred unit).
  Loading + error + empty states preserved (no changes to control flow).
  PWA meta-tag effect, command mutation flow, sub-component signatures (StatusIcon, WatchPWAMeta),
  state badge classes, and lucide icons all unchanged.
  Hardcoded English strings ("just now", "m ago", "h ago", "d ago", "m to full", "No vehicle found")
  are PRE-EXISTING and not in the SI-port scope; deferred per Phase-43/0034 NOTES precedent.
=== I18N ===
en.json: NO CHANGES
  Page does not currently use i18n at all (chrome-less wearable surface). My SI changes do not
