=== NOTES ===
1. SCOPE: Pure SI-conversion port of the single-page WatchFacePage. Hook + i18n untouched.
   Same atomic shape as Phase-43/0023 (BatteryHealthPage) — boundary-conversion-only.

2. PRE-EXISTING BACKEND BUG NOT FIXED: watch_handler.go:244-245 reads
   ratedRange, _ := signalFloat(signals, "RatedRange"); rangeKm := ratedRange * 1.60934
   If RatedRange has been Phase-42 normalize.toSI'd to meters in redis (per ADR-004 #4 +
   routing.yaml UnitKindDistance routing of all distance signals), this multiplier produces
   rangeKm = meters * 1.60934, which is a 1609x inflation when the raw signal is already SI
   meters. Frontend trusts the documented wire shape (range_km field name) and applies
   convertDistanceFromSI(km*1000, pref) — locked-policy precedent from Phase-43/0035
   share_handler.go bug deferral and Phase-43/0030 MaintenancePage deferral. A backend-only
   prompt that can touch internal/api/watch_handler.go is required to verify whether
   RatedRange in redis is meters or miles and adjust the scaling accordingly.

3. WatchSummaryWidget.tsx (web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/, OUT OF SCOPE) reads
   summary.range_km and summary.inside_temp_c via the inline WatchSummary interface from
   useWatch.ts. Wire shape is unchanged so the widget continues to function. The widget
   also uses the legacy useSettings.kmToMiles + convertTemp pattern which is the same
   pre-existing condition as on this page; widget migration belongs to a future
   features/dashboard/widgets sweep prompt that is not yet scheduled.

4. WatchSummary type kept INLINE in useWatch.ts (NOT moved to web/src/api/types.ts). Two
   consumers — WatchFacePage and WatchSummaryWidget — both import via
   `import { useWatchSummary } from '@/api/hooks/useWatch'` and read fields off the hook's
   return type, so the type only needs to live with the hook. Same precedent as
   Phase-43/0036 OnboardingStatus.

5. i18n NOT introduced. Page is chrome-less for 40-45mm wearable displays and currently
   uses zero i18n (hardcoded English: "just now", "m ago", "h ago", "d ago", "m to full",
   "No vehicle found"). My SI changes added no new English strings — the unit suffix is
   the user's preference value (km/mi/ft) and the temperature uses a bare degree glyph.
   Adding i18n broadly would expand scope beyond an SI port (Phase-43/0034+0035 precedent).

6. BatteryGauge prop signature CHANGED: rangeKm: number -> rangeDisplay: number +
   distanceUnit: DistanceUnitPref. The component now receives an already-converted display
   number plus the user's preferred unit suffix. This keeps the SI conversion at the page
   boundary (single source of truth) and lets the gauge stay presentational.

7. Backend `outside_temp_c` and `charge_rate` are exposed on the WatchSummary wire shape
   but the page does NOT display them. No conversion needed for unrendered fields.
   `time_to_full` is already in minutes (backend ttf*60 in watch_handler.go:253), so the
   `Math.round(data.time_to_full)m to full` text is correct as-is.

8. PowerShell-7 quirks reused from prior Phase-43 prompts:
   (a) Resolve-Path absolute on $log BEFORE Push-Location web else Tee-Object loses the
       file under web/.github/* during BUILD (Phase-46/64 fix);
   (b) .\node_modules\.bin\tsc.cmd + npm.cmd run build instead of npx tsc + npm run build
       to dodge npm 10's executable-resolution quirk under pwsh -File invocation
       (Phase-43/0021 fix);
   (c) Self-deleting gate via Remove-Item $ScriptPath BEFORE git status check else the
       gate script trips the disallowed-file check (Phase-46/65 fix);
   (d) git status --porcelain parsed by Substring(3) + -like "$prefix*" instead of
       regex.Escape on Windows backslash paths because porcelain output uses forward
       slashes (Phase-43/0033 NOTES);
   (e) Audit regex uses single-quoted PowerShell ['"] character class instead of the
       prompt's verbatim ['`""\""] doubled-escape sequence which mis-parses under
       pwsh -File (Phase-43/0034+0035 NOTES);
   (f) Long log appends written via temp file + Get-Content | Add-Content because the
       prompt body's degree symbol + backtick characters trigger PowerShell's "Unicode
       escape sequence" parser at degree-symbol + backtick boundary (e.g., the original
       attempt to write `unitPrefs.distance` in a here-string failed with
       "The Unicode escape sequence is not valid").
